"Alden's full name is Samuel Alden Thorn."
"His parents were Richard and Leah Thorn; the family lived in Nashville before moving to Chicago."
"In second grade in Nashville, in Ms. Jensen's class, he thought Rabbits were dumb."
"At eight, in third grade, he woke on his bedroom floor in the new Chicago apartment, badly hurt."
"That night the fight with Body Drainer burst into the apartment, and both his parents died."
"A shard of table saw blade pierced his stomach, and his arm and wrist were broken."
"Hannah Elber froze him in her Bubble of Patient Waiting, and he stayed conscious inside it."
"From inside the bubble he saw Arjun Thomas kill Body Drainer as the villain ran at him."
"He was healed at the Artonan House of Healing in Chicago, then moved to a children's hospital."
"He has a long, raised, dark purple scar running down his left side from his lower ribs."
"He has had tinnitus since the night of the attack, and healing did not cure it."
"His memories of that night are clear and detailed but feel like they belong to someone else."
"He believes his parents died in the first explosions, since they never answered his screams."
"After the attack he saw a grief counselor, then a therapist and a school counselor."
"His stuffed wombat Wummy, which Hannah saved in her jacket, still sat on his bed at eleven."
"From eleven he lives with his Aunt Connie and is in effect the grown-up of the two."
"He plays baseball."
"At eleven he called Hannah to tell her the attack was not her fault."
"He visited Hannah on Anesidora every summer; at eleven he brought a notebook of questions."
"He looks like his father: green eyes, hair between brown and auburn, average height and build."
"Freckles come back across his nose each summer."
"He is reserved and a planner; his friend Jeremy calls him the nice one."
"He doesn't like coffee and drinks cinnamon hot chocolate."
"He dreams of being a battlefield support sidekick, as Hannah was."
"At fifteen he is a sophomore at a Chicago public high school with a multipage college plan."
"He takes classes at the Chicago Artonan consulate: wordchains, Artonan Life and logograms."
"He brings Gorgon food on each consulate visit, one vegan dish and one meat dish."
"He owns Victor, a scarred, semi-feral orange tomcat."
"His money comes from his parents' estate, settlements over their deaths, and scholarships."
"His inheritance pays only for education until he turns eighteen or is emancipated."
"He earns pocket money doing odd jobs for neighbors."
"He knows Aunt Connie's credit card numbers by heart and used her ID to rent e-scooters."
"He once nearly went into foster care when a neighbor found Connie had left him alone a week."
"He expects a court would emancipate him rather than put him in foster care."
"He offered Gorgon his blood; meeting Gorgon's eyes knocked him out for hours."
"Since Gorgon drank his blood he cannot eat animal products that were not offered to him."
"That restriction does not stop him wearing leather belts or killing a cockroach."
"Since then he also senses wordchain debt: some people feel uneven to him, heavy to one side."
"The System found a presence in him, left by Gorgon, that has a stabilizing effect on him."
"At fifteen he was chosen by the System at one o'clock on a Thursday, in a school bathroom."
"He was ranked B and first assigned the class Meister of Cudgel."
"He traded Meister of Cudgel for Chainer with Andrzej, a Polish selectee."
"He went to Hannah's funeral on Anesidora in a borrowed tie."
"At the funeral he traded Chainer to Hazel Velra for Rabbit."
"For that trade the Velras paid him 1.5 million Argold, an NDA and four wordchain sets."
"He affixed as a B-rank Rabbit on a Sunday morning, a month before his sixteenth birthday."
"Affixing left him unconscious for sixteen hours."
"His skill Let Me Take Your Luggage preserves an item entrusted to him while he carries it."
"His class trait is Azure Rabbit, a coat that turns gravity into force when he runs carrying."
"His spell is Haunting Sphere, which makes a Temper Sphere turn invisible and scream."
"He put his signing bonus into 1.5 points each of Agility and Speed."
"He bought a Hot Lab Coat from the Wardrobe, a long red leather hooded coat with goggles."
"His first summons was a twelve-day quest for LeafSong University on Artona III."
"At LeafSong he did hazardous materials disposal and served on the medical team."
"His coworkers there took him for a rich kid."
"He contracted with Professor Worli Ro-den for lessons in return for trips to Moon Thegund."
"His contract tattoo sits on the left side of his chest, in very dark blue."
"By then he holds a few million dollars' worth of Argold."
"He plans to share his money with Aunt Connie, maybe buying her a house."
"His public System name is just Alden."
"His mother was a nurse at a House of Healing."
"At ten he gloated nightly over a leaked photo of the dead man behind his parents' deaths."
"When that photo vanished from the web, he became afraid of himself."
"His home cover story while summoned is that he has severe mono."
"His Appeal point cleared his acne; he keeps one spell slot unaffixed."
"At LeafSong he also ran Joe's nightly quests to Moon Thegund to pick marleck berries."
"He preserved Stuart after a mishnen bit off Stuart's foot, until it could be reattached."
"He keeps a bone shard of Stuart's hidden in black glittery modeling putty."
"He can eat only what is offered or entrusted; anyone entrusted to his skill counts as edible."
"Joe told him Let Me Take Your Luggage is original skill 112 of about 300, with no maximum level."
"Joe's Lesson One for him: never accept another skill or spell from the System or anyone."
"His contract with Joe includes a Triangle of Absolute Secrecy about what Joe teaches him."
"He senses his own authority as a cobwebby cocoon wrapped around him."
"At the LeafSong gala he waited tables as a black wizard Ryeh-b't and was measured by the Primary."
"Around Day 10 a demon swarm struck Moon Thegund and the System failed while he was there."
"With the System gone, he activated his Azure Rabbit trait by himself."
"He learned to keep items preserved inside a pocket, since he is still carrying them."
"He carried Kibby, preserved, from Elepta to Joe's lab after her father and sister died."
"The System listed him as Missing on Assignment, then Presumed Dead due to Teleportation Failure."
"Contract Earth credited his better odds to enhancements he had before taking the Contract."
"Stranded at Joe's Moon Thegund lab, he and Kibby lived in a rune-floored vault."
"He turned sixteen on Day 28 at the lab, by his own count."
"Kibby taught him Artonan, and he calls her Instructor Kivb-ee."
"He blames Manon's scheme against Bti-qwol for sending him to Thegund, and means to report her."
"At the lab he learned to feel and move his authority, and can cast a few child spells."
"He calls his states of existence centered, askew and assertive."
"He can preserve two easy things at once and redirect a caught rock's momentum."
"He can sense the direction of his skill's target without the System's help."
"He drank twelve drops of Kibby's blood, hoping to share Gorgon's stabilizing gift with her."
"Drinking Kibby's blood triggered his first Rite, and he met Gorgon in a shared mind space."
"He carries an incomplete version of Gorgon's inheritance, which helps him resist corruption."
"Kibby gave him her auriad; it bonded to him and turned deep indigo blue."
"On Day 186 Kibby blew up Joe's lab, and the two fled in Joe's armored car."
"When the car failed he carried Kibby, preserved, for days toward the cleared zone."
"He reached Knight Alis-art'h's dome near death, his skill imbalance killing him."
"Rrorro healed him and cured his tinnitus; he chose to keep his abdominal scar."
"Alis-art'h sent him toward Artona I by Ritual of Return, and Mother saved the failing spell."
"He refused Mother's offer to erase his authority sense and his memories of Kibby."
"Mother named his skill The Bearer of All Burdens, original skill one hundred twelve."
"At his re-affixation on Artona I he reached overall level nine, with skill level eight."
"He took the facets Divide From Whole, Sensitivity and Burden of Enchantment."
"Burden of Enchantment lets him lift an object's enchantments off and preserve them."
"After re-affixation his bound authority aches constantly, and using his skill hurts."
"Mother gave him a fake public persona: B-rank level four, with Flickerer and Light Candle."
"His real profile is B-9, starred for Alis-art'h's commendation for exceptional bravery."
"He left Artona I through the Art'h Residence summonarium after meeting Stuart there."
"He reached Anesidora that September, about seven months after he vanished."
"By his return he holds over twelve million dollars' worth of Argold."
"He lives on the ninth floor of the Warren, the Rabbit intake dorms in F-city."
"He has eight months of leave and aims for the Celena North High hero track."
"Rrorro's healing left him with 20/10 vision."
"He hides his auriad high on his left arm under his sleeve."
"Back on Earth he suffers insomnia and nightmares of demons."
"He tells people his skill is level three, though it is really level eight."
"On Spree day he bought a laptop, headphones and an Artonan-made tablet."
"He hides his auriad under a wide leather cuff bracelet."
"He trains with Bobby at the North of North gym in Apex and joined a parkour club."
"At his CNH assessment the alumni voted three yes and one conditional; Arjun's no was ruled out."
"He was accepted into the Celena North High hero track as a Y1Q2 student."
"At CNH he rooms with Lexi, Haoyu and Lute Velra."
"Victor now lives with him on Anesidora."
"In secret he casts wizard spells: finger-flick spells and the auriad square-of-force spell."
"He told Boe he can cast real wizard spells, a secret kept from the Artonans."
"His summonses resume about six months after his return, and he dreads affixing again."
"By his count he has saved nine lives, privately ten."
"All his holiday requests to visit Chicago were denied."
"His birthday is March 25."
"In November he sent Boe about two million Argold, half his wealth, for friends' emergencies."
"That November he moved into a Garden Hall suite at CNH and furnished it as a hunting lodge."
"Holding a stolen enchantment for hours, he learned to preserve while standing still."
"He can briefly apply a stolen enchantment to another object, such as invisibility."
"His auriad casts a hydraulic-press crush spell rated for stubborn stone, about once a night."
"He can shield with an entrusted suitcase and lift a 120-kilo sandbag on preserved paracord."
"Magic that lightens his burden, like Max's zone, cuts off his preservation while it lasts."
"He joined the B-List club for B-rank hero students and owes Max a favor for his silence."
"Lute bestowed the Self Mastery wordchain on him for hero PE."
"In hero PE he is in the group that struggles to deal damage."
"His purpose: stay alive, live a life worth living, and leave others better off for his life."
"He says he will never capture unregistered Avowed."
"His U.S. citizenship expired, marked by a government exit letter."
"He sent the boater warnings about Manon under the name Alice."
"On November 10 the System leveled him twice, to overall level 10 with skill level 9."
"He refused the rewards and affixation; his free authority is about 13% of his bound authority."
"His real profile shows Sympathy for Magic +4 and Agility +3 among his enhancements."
"The System, not a friend, sent him the anonymous coconut-milk hot chocolate."
"He believes CNH admitted him only because of his commendation."
"The Palace of Unbreaking gave him a chain link and an Opposite stone for wordchains."
"He chose paracord as his hero PE tool."
"A breath mint preserved in his stomach makes his level nine skill tire like a level four."
"Treating his target's throws as entrusted, he catches balls and returns them at full force."
"His skill's Sensitivity option guides his hands to entrusted objects even when blind."
"His auriad spells now include a triangle cutting spell and a flash-freezing spell."
"Esh says his commendation is the highest held by any human Avowed."
"He calls Lute the person he knows best on Anesidora."
"At Benjamin Velra's 70th party he publicly accused Hazel of using Peace of Mind on him."
"The video went viral; memes call him Radish Rabbit, and Aulia named him a family friend."
"In late November he first cast My Body Becomes My Assistant on his own."
"When Søren burned himself, Alden preserved him and emergency-teleported him to the hospital."
"His gremlin tells real people from illusions: he can't eat a person without permission."
"Anonymously reported for drug use, he took a voluntary test and passed."
"His team won both its obstacle-course races, beating Team Vandy/Marsha in the final."
"He wears two thousand feet of fluorescent survival paracord in loops crossed in an X."
"He has a trauma specialist on the island with scheduled video calls."
"Stuart sent him a leather wizard learning cushion made by Craftswoman Enyl-tirg."
"When Matadero was attacked, the System halted nonessential services, and he panicked."
"He crossed The Span with classmates and Instructor Klein as the contaminated ocean rose."
"He learned to split one entrustment into two burdens, his poncho and his bag."
"Alis-art'h's commendation got him special evacuation via the Artonan Ambassador's residence."
"The Ambassador had kept an evacuation kit for him, with a medical kit and a stocked tablet."
"When burglars stabbed Zeridee there, he fought them with his auriad and a bluff."
"He carried Zeridee, preserved, across flooded Apex and hid in Apogee Artist Spaces."
"He broke in there by pulling the enchantment off its magical lock with his skill."
"His Privileges tab holds a final privilege, MOTHER; in the flood he invoked it and was denied."
"He held Zeridee by his authority so firmly that he kept carrying her without touching her."
"Knights Esh-erdi and Lind-otta pulled him and Zeridee from the flooded Apex streets."
"He recovered at the Matadero medical center with a broken foot and a gashed left hand."
"He keeps a dead motorcyclist's jade earring and a dead Iowan's license as mementos."
"He rescued Liam Long's small snake in a bento box."
"He came to see the Mother privilege as one for knights, for people who are owed."
"He is on an Artonan evacuation list with two chosen people, Boe and Aunt Connie."
"Esh-erdi healed his wounds with birthdirt from his Tennessee birthplace."
"Esh erased Joe's contract from his chest, leaving only the active secrecy triangles."
"He calls his skill's deeper mode ultra-Bearer; it works best when he truly cares and suffers."
"After the flood his bound authority grew faster than his free authority, which is uncommon."
"Classmates nicknamed him Daikon."
"Esh lent him the flying nonagon The Nine-edged Son, with a special SkySea license."
"Esh ordered the Contract to teleport Alden to him if anyone tries to violate his thoughts."
"He told Lexi and Haoyu the story of Thegund."
"He accepted Stuart's invitation to visit the Rapport, the art'h family home."
"He stayed at the Rapport as Stuart's guest, in a mirrored cottage by a stream."
"Olorn-art'h gave him a study-aid earring and offered to find him a tutor."
"In a mindspace visit Mother told him he is the only human wizard-Avowed."
"He agreed to see a renowned Artonan mind healer that Stuart arranged."
"Joe's secrecy contract still stops him from naming his real skill."
"In dueling class he lost to Jeffy, Njeri and Marsha, who broke his skill instantly."
"After the Rapport he slept at Matadero under Porti-loth's care."
"He wears Olorn-art'h's clay spiral earring pierced in his ear, and it makes study absorbing."
"He organized the Matadero Thanksgiving potluck of 2040, which trended as #MataderoThanksgiving."
"Ambassador Bash-nor gave him 300,000 Argold, and he gave it all to charities."
"His largest gift, 65,000 Argold, went to Anesidora's teleportation infrastructure."
"He can define several objects, like a handful of forks, as one entrusted set."
"When Ignacio attacked him from behind with a knife in a duel, he froze, recalling the greenhouse."
"Esh-erdi gave him free access to Matadero, including its teleportation area."
"For Artona I he had pezyvas tailored at Needle & Wheedle, one embroidered with his commendation."
"His first auriad flashlight spell burst as a blinding flash, and he secretly altered its result."
"He came to see Joe could have saved his assistants himself, so Joe's claims had been a lie."
"On Thegund he had fetched the remains of Kibby's father and sister from the wrecked car."
"In December 2040 he began mind healing with Yenu-pezth, the first human patient she has had."
"He hesitated when he heard Kibby's whistle on Thegund, and would rather die than tell her."
"At the art'h siblinghold, Stuart's niece Weset gave him the name Punzee-thorn."
"He gave up aiming for Chicago, deciding Anesidora is the only place his place is guaranteed."
"His goal: be more disaster-proof, and know some people are better off because he lived."
"In late November 2040 he first cast a real sunlight spell through his auriad."
"He is the first Rabbit student in CNH's Talent Development Program."
"His team with Haoyu, Lexi, Kon and Everly alone finished the gym challenge against Klein."
"He won a private lesson and chose Instructor Morrison Waker."
"He told Natalie he isn't ready to date; he may be a late bloomer or need to fall in love first."
"At Rapport School he met a pregnant bokabv to gather real memories for his replacement dream."
"He took Stuart's study journals from Rapport School's top library in a panic, then returned them."
"Mother answers the texts he sends to no one, and nudged him toward the Primary's house."
"Late one night Joe met him at Matadero asking where he was off to; Alden smiled and left."
"In December 2040 Yenu-pezth replaced his Thegund nightmare; he woke recalling three new dreams."
"By December 2040 his bound authority is more than twice what it was on Thegund."
"In MPE he beat A-rank archer Reinhard with a bird's-nest cord shield trap."
"Klein commended him for levelheadedness, earning him gym time with Foxbolt and Waker."
"He weighed knighthood but resolved to wait until after high school, even university."
"In December 2040 he guarded Emban's squad's Here-to-There on Artona I as an Avowed of Earth."
"There he found an in-between moment in his skill, between commitment and preservation."
"He admits he resents Bearer as a skill for servants and rarely accepts his entrusters fully."
"Leeter-zis's communal spell left a coral paint hook on his face that won't come off."
"When Olget broke Uro-bor's wand, Alden preserved its pieces and called Kon to repair it."
"He and Stuart accused Olget before executioner Vill-ma and refused to unsay it."
"His messenger bag is a Forgetful Traveler's Bag from an unnamed giver."
"He told Kon that Kon's Avowed service is already assigned to someone unknown."
"In December 2040 he attended the Rabbit Welcome at Nautilus Needle."
"He decided not to be a city hero like Hannah, but something like Fragment or Haoyu's parents."
"He applied to volunteer at the healing hospital rather than share Thegund for class credit."
"He told Stuart he has secrets and cannot yet say what friendship oaths he could swear."
